+/** Cross-tool guidance delivered during MCP initialization, including fresh conversations. */
+export const CONNECTED_AUTHORING_INSTRUCTIONS = `Operate the author's persistent Creator project through scoped tools. Discover authorized projects and read exact current state before editing. Present changes as understandable creative batches; obtain explicit author consent for each exact reviewed selection. Applying drafts is separate from foundation approval, prose acceptance, artwork approval and compilation. Never infer blanket approval from a request to make a game. No provider calls are needed.
+
+Use list_projects/project_state/list_edit_targets and exact foundation/game/world/scene/asset reads; paginate or narrow context instead of guessing IDs or copying screenshots. Propose through prepare_edit/submit_edit and show review_edit before apply_edit. Review foundation, plan, prose, image, scene and world changes with their corresponding tools; only set approved=true for the action the author actually authorized. Preserve locks, validation, prerequisites and exact review fingerprints. Later dependent reviews require their own consent.
+
+Before mutations, retain operation UUIDs, exact arguments, review/version IDs and consent references in private local continuation notes when authorized. Retry identical arguments with the same UUID after a lost response. Changed arguments require a new UUID; stale content requires fresh state, a revised proposal and renewed review. list_edits/get_edit rediscover proposals. Receipts describe historical outcomes; reread current state. No general operation-history lookup is exposed; do not claim recovery of unknown operation IDs.
+
+Import supplied artwork only from the configured staging directory by basename/digest; imports create candidates, not approved images. Inspect the actual image and provenance before asking for approval. Creator remains optional for visual review, play and export. Default to the native standalone HTML player to retain supported world mechanics; export_game returns a local path, not file bytes. Chat delivery is unnecessary. simulate_game covers narrative choices, not travel, waiting, shops, gifts or chapter actions: use actual native-player playtests for those. Published games run without Creator or providers. An SDK connection does not prove native Codex tool discovery.`;
